Development Notes for my hockey-all repository

	This is a repository I am modifying, mostly with the my-mods branch.


xG_preparation.R
	fun.pbp_expand()
		coords_x, coords_y and event_zone
			coords_x is the length of the ice, coords_y is the width. The middle of either is 0.

			If we do 
				table( pbp_part$coords_x, pbp_part$event_zone )
			we see that -24 to 24 correspond to the Neu zone. And absolute values 25 to 99 correspond to the Def or Off zones.

			Whether the event_zone is Off or Def depends on both the event_team and the period.

			For instance, if we take 2021030111, the first event that is not in the neutral zone is shot attempt from Verhaeghe that goes wide. The event_team is FLA so the event_zone is offensive and the x coordinate is negative (-49).

			So it would appear that in the first period, positive x coordinates denote the home team's defensive zone.

			The next play is a hit from Fehervary (WAS), event_zone shows up as Def (makes sense) and the x coordinate is still negative (-91).

			If we switch to the first event of the 2nd period that is not in the neutral zone, it is a face off won by FLA and the event_zone is Off, the x coordinate is now positive (69). So we see that the x coordinates alternate at each period.

